  <!-- 3. 24-48H DELTA -->
  <div class="section" id="delta">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      What Moved (Last 24-48h)
      <span class="meta">Descriptive · banned-verb lint enforced · each paragraph cites a forecast or is marked context-only</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="delta-narrative">
      <p>CENTCOM struck three Iranian crude oil tankers in the Gulf of Oman on September 5, including M/T Kylo (also identified as M/T Noxen), which CENTCOM described as part of a multibillion-dollar shadow network funding IRGC operations and regional proxies (CENTCOM official release; ABC News). No US servicemembers were injured. This is the second CENTCOM kinetic action against Iranian-linked shipping within five days, following the September 1 strikes on IRGC targets inside Iran. → supports <span class="cite">F6</span> without move</p>
      <p>The IRGC Navy attacked three oil tankers transiting what it called an "unauthorized route" in the Strait of Hormuz and targeted three US-affiliated vessels elsewhere in the region on September 5; neither US vessel sustained damage (CENTCOM). AIS-tracked commercial transits in the Strait of Hormuz remained at 4–11 vessels per day on September 4–5, continuing the multi-week low-traffic period well below the 30-vessel threshold. The Sep 5 IRGC actions occurred against the backdrop of IRGC Khatam Al Anbiya's September 3 confirmed mine redeployment (Maham-3/7 series, per OSINT tracking). → supports <span class="cite">F4</span> without move</p>
      <p>VP Vance stated on September 4 that the US would hold "no talks with Tehran until it stops shooting at commercial shipping." No named Iranian official from the Foreign Ministry, SNSC, or Supreme Leader's office issued a fresh statement committing to or seeking mediated talks through the September 5-6 evidence window. Oman and Qatar messaging channels remained open per background diplomatic sourcing (The Hill), but no session date exists and no mediator readout claimed a breakthrough. → supports <span class="cite">F3</span> without move</p>
      <p>Israeli election polling: Haaretz published a poll on August 9 showing Likud recovering to 24 seats (ahead of Yashar at 23), while a September 3 Haaretz poll showed Likud at 21 (behind Yashar at 22). No new poll was published in the September 4–6 window. The alternating 1-3 seat margin has persisted across five consecutive polls; both blocs remain at 52-53 seats well below the 61-seat coalition threshold. 51 days remain to the October 27 election date. → supports <span class="cite">F5</span> without move</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 4. SCENARIO MAP -->
