        <span class="iran-media-badge">Kayhan</span>
      </div>
      <p>IRNA and Press TV on September 5 ran extended coverage of President Pezeshkian's September 1 SCO conditional offer ("if the US returns to its MOU commitments, Iran will immediately reciprocate"), framing the offer as proof that Iran had "already extended a hand of peace" while the United States chose escalation by striking Iranian tankers in international waters. No new statement from Araghchi, the SNSC, or the Supreme Leader's office on talks readiness appeared in the September 5-6 monitoring window. → supports <span class="cite">F3</span> without move</p>
      <p>Tasnim on September 5 characterized CENTCOM's destruction of three Iranian crude tankers as "piracy against Iranian national property" and cited Foreign Ministry spokesperson Esmaeil Baqaei calling for international condemnation of the strikes, framing the CENTCOM action as a violation of international maritime law. Kayhan's editorial described the tanker strikes as "an act of war against the civilian economy." Neither outlet ran any reporting on internal deliberation over returning to talks. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
      <p>Fars News ran a photo essay of IRGC naval patrol operations in the Persian Gulf on September 5 without accompanying text commentary. IRGC commander Salami's standing statement that "Iran's deterrence infrastructure remains fully functional" was re-syndicated across all state channels following the September 5 bilateral exchange, with no named official contradicting the posture of continued military resistance. → supports <span class="cite">F6</span> without move</p>
    </div>
  </div>

