        <span class="p">8–15%</span>
        <div class="drivers">Active US military strikes have degraded IRGC naval and logistics infrastructure since February 28. Economic stress from the Hormuz blockade and war-risk insurance exit is severe. However, elite cohesion within the IRGC and clerical establishment has not fractured publicly; the "resistance" frame has consolidated rather than fragmented mass opinion. Historical base rate: Iran survived the 8-year Iraq War and sanctions cycles without regime transition. The 12-month window (to ~Sep 2027) is too short for economic pressure alone to produce collapse absent internal elite fracture or a catastrophic military defeat neither currently observable. Last updated: 2026-09-06.</div>
